# ==============================================================================
# 🎸 2. ROCKSTAR GAMES & AAA STUDIO TOOLS CODING STANDARDS
# ==============================================================================
# When writing or modifying Blender Python scripts or pipeline runners:
# 1. AAA Pipeline Standards:
#    - Serialize runtime animation tracks with Unit Quaternions [w, x, y, z] and velocity vectors.
#    - Support both Blender native (Z-up) and Game Engine swizzled (Y-up: X, Z, -Y) coordinates.
#    - Integrate real-time microsecond telemetry profiling (time.perf_counter() + tracemalloc).
#    - Build standalone CLI batch runners (pipeline_batch_runner.py) for headless CI/CD automation.
# 2. Broadcast Sandwich Typography:
#    - Top Kicker (+Y = +0.58m), Hero Center (Y = 0.00m), Sponsor Anchor (-Y = -0.58m).
#    - Camera-normal pitch alignment (61.74°) guaranteeing 0.26+ screen-height air gaps.
# 3. Balanced Centered Exits:
#    - BURST_FORWARD, CENTER_IMPLODE, DROP_DOWN, LIFT_UP strictly locked to X = 0.0 and rot_z = 0.0°.
# 4. Technical Artist UX:
#    - Visual 3D motion trajectory splines in the viewport with color-coded velocity arcs.
#    - Anti-glare LED diode protection: Laurier Gold (#FDB913), Deep Purple (#20003B), NO pure white strokes.

# ==============================================================================
# ⚔️ 3. C++ WASM & LOW-LEVEL ENGINE STANDARDS (light-years-game)
# ==============================================================================
# 1. Custom Fixed-Timestep Loop: Decouple physics ticks from rendering frame rate.
# 2. Zero Unnecessary Heap Allocations: Use contiguous object pooling and spatial hashing.
# 3. Emscripten WASM target: Keep code strictly compliant with C++17/20 standards.
